"},{"date":"2026-09-08","committee":"Cabinet","time":"1.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://moderngov.stoke.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-09","committee":"Housing, Regeneration & Operations Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"10.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://moderngov.stoke.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-10","committee":"City Council","time":"2.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://moderngov.stoke.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-17","committee":"Children and Family Services Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"10.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://moderngov.stoke.gov.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Strategic IT Development capital reduced by \u00a31.5m (60%) with potential ongoing slippage","lead":"Strategic IT infrastructure delays can cascade through operations; uncertainty about digital transformation investment at Q1 signals resource or prioritisation constraints","iso":"2026-08-11","paper_title":"Annex Fii - 2026-27 Cap Inv Prg - FO Summary and Detail - Qtr 1","paper_url":"https://moderngov.stoke.gov.uk/documents/s182427/182427.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"HRA fire safety and building compliance capital slipped by \u00a39m; only \u00a32.9m of \u00a311.9m Apartments/Compliance/Fire Safety budget forecast to be spent","lead":"Fire safety and regulatory compliance work on housing is safety-critical; delay of \u00a39m in this area signals either governance issues or financial constraints in council housing maintenance, creating potential liability and regulatory risk","iso":"2026-08-11","paper_title":"Annex Fii - 2026-27 Cap Inv Prg - FO Summary and Detail - Qtr 1","paper_url":"https://moderngov.stoke.gov.uk/documents/s182427/182427.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Adult Social Care Supported Living project entirely deferred (\u00a34m capital write-off for year)","lead":"Full deferral of planned adult social care capital signals either funding constraints or project delays affecting planned accommodation provision and service capacity","iso":"2026-08-11","paper_title":"Annex Fii - 2026-27 Cap Inv Prg - FO Summary and Detail - Qtr 1","paper_url":"https://moderngov.stoke.gov.uk/documents/s182427/182427.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-08-11","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Annex Fii - 2026-27 Cap Inv Prg - FO Summary and Detail - Qtr 1","paper_url":"https://moderngov.stoke.gov.uk/documents/s182427/182427.pdf","headline":"Strategic IT Development capital reduced by \u00a31.5m (60%) with potential ongoing slippage","detail":"Chief Executive Directorate Strategic IT Development budgeted at \u00a32.5m but forecast at \u00a31m, a \u00a31.5m variance. Council flags potential slippage with proposals to be confirmed during the year.","category":"capital","matters":"Strategic IT infrastructure delays can cascade through operations; uncertainty about digital transformation investment at Q1 signals resource or prioritisation constraints","figures":"Budget \u00a32,500k, Forecast \u00a31,000k, Variance (\u00a31,500k)","quote":"Potential slippage on Strategic IT Development. Proposals to be confirmed during the year, forecast outturn will be monitored and updated each quarter.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-08-11","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Annex Fii - 2026-27 Cap Inv Prg - FO Summary and Detail - Qtr 1","paper_url":"https://moderngov.stoke.gov.uk/documents/s182427/182427.pdf","headline":"HRA fire safety and building compliance capital slipped by \u00a39m; only \u00a32.9m of \u00a311.9m Apartments/Compliance/Fire Safety budget forecast to be spent","detail":"Housing Revenue Account shows \u00a313.6m underspend (20% variance). Largest single component is Apartments, Compliance & Fire Safety: budgeted \u00a311.9m but forecast \u00a32.9m only (\u00a39m shortfall). Council attributes to design stage delays with plan of works to be reviewed in Q2. Decent Homes also \u00a33.9m underspent.","category":"capital","matters":"Fire safety and regulatory compliance work on housing is safety-critical; delay of \u00a39m in this area signals either governance issues or financial constraints in council housing maintenance, creating potential liability and regulatory risk","figures":"HRA total variance (\u00a313,573k); Apartments/Compliance/Fire Safety budget \u00a311,883k, forecast \u00a32,914k, variance (\u00a38,969k); Decent Homes budget \u00a321,530k, forecast \u00a317,631k, variance (\u00a33,899k)","quote":"Homes England grant received in Quarter 1, plan of works to be reviewed and budgets potentially to be re-profiled during Quarter 2. Other slippages are due to delays in the design stages of some projects.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-08-11","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Annex Fii - 2026-27 Cap Inv Prg - FO Summary and Detail - Qtr 1","paper_url":"https://moderngov.stoke.gov.uk/documents/s182427/182427.pdf","headline":"Adult Social Care Supported Living project entirely deferred (\u00a34m capital write-off for year)","detail":"Supported Living - Step Up Step Down capital project budgeted at \u00a34m has zero forecast outturn at Q1. No delivery is expected in 2026/27, with the council noting a review is underway and proposals to be confirmed.","category":"capital","matters":"Full deferral of planned adult social care capital signals either funding constraints or project delays affecting planned accommodation provision and service capacity","figures":"Budget \u00a34,000k, Forecast \u00a30k, Variance (\u00a34,000k)","quote":"Review underway in relation to Supported Living - Step Up Step Down, forecast outturn will be monitored and updated each quarter.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-08-11","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Annex Fii - 2026-27 Cap Inv Prg - FO Summary and Detail - Qtr 1","paper_url":"https://moderngov.stoke.gov.uk/documents/s182427/182427.pdf","headline":"Commercial Development capital project reduced by \u00a316.5m (71%) with no confirmed scope or direction","detail":"Resources Directorate Commercial Development budget of \u00a323m reduced to \u00a36.5m forecast, a \u00a316.5m variance at Q1. The council states a review is underway with proposals to be confirmed during the year and outturn monitored quarterly. This represents a material uncommitted reduction in planned investment with no stated recovery plan.","category":"capital","matters":"Commercial investment underspends with unconfirmed direction signal either delayed regeneration investment or scope reduction; this level of uncertainty on \u00a316.5m is material for cash planning and lender risk assessment","figures":"Budget \u00a323,000k, Forecast \u00a36,500k, Variance (\u00a316,500k)","quote":"Review underway in relation to Commercial Development, proposals to be confirmed during the year, forecast outturn will be monitored and updated each quarter.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-08-11","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Annex C - 2026-27 Strategic Contingency - Qtr 1","paper_url":"https://moderngov.stoke.gov.uk/documents/s182421/182421.pdf","headline":"Council has committed \u00a310,000 for an external financial improvement adviser in 2026/27","detail":"The s151 Officer has approved funding for an external financial improvement adviser as a strategic contingency commitment in 2026/27. This was approved in consultation with the Cabinet Member for Finance.","category":"governance","matters":"An external improvement adviser appointment signals that the council's finance leadership recognizes areas where external expertise is required, which would be of concern to a lender assessing the council's financial management capability and capacity to manage debt.","figures":"\u00a310,000 approved in 2026/27","quote":"External Financial Improvement Adviser  (10)","material":false}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-08-13"},"name":"Stoke-on-Trent UA","findings_total":99,"news_drafts_total":3}}